    <briefdescription>
<para>I/O operation interrupted error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1IOInterruptedError" kindref="compound">IOInterruptedError</ref> represents an error when an I/O operation is interrupted (e.g., by a signal like EINTR).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>IOInterruptedError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;I/O<sp/>interrupted&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>IOInterruptedError(&quot;Read<sp/>interrupted<sp/>by<sp/>signal&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
